{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "The Good Old Days"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "How Things Have Changed"}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 8}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Identify and describe events in a range of social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations. "}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "mindset"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the set of attitudes held by someone "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I think the mindset was very different from today."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le08ob07aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about social activities."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "protective"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "wanting to protect someone or something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Our parents were very protective of us."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le08ob07aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to sneak "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to secretly do something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: My friends used to sneak out of the house"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le08ob07aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "wholesome"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "innocent; healthy "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective):"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It was exciting but it was very wholesome."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le08ob07aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "boundary"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a limit of a subject or area of activity "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Social media accounts give kids no boundaries within which to function."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le08ob07aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "limit"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "boundary "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Being a teenager is about pushing boundaries and testing limits, right?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le08ob07aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Adjectives About Feelings and Reactions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You talk about feelings and reactions using adjectives.  It is important to use the correct kind of adjective - it is common for English language learners to confuse the two kinds of adjectives when talking about feelings and reactions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "1. -ed adjectives"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Adjectives that end in <span class=\"strong\">-ed </span> are used to describe how a person <span class=\"strong\"> feels</span>, like <span class=\"italic\">annoyed</span>, <span class=\"italic\"> fascinated</span>, <span class=\"italic\"> entertained</span>, <span class=\"italic\"> surprised</span>, <span class=\"italic\"> worried </span> or <span class=\"italic\"> tired </span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">I am annoyed.<br/>Parents are thrilled.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "2. -ing adjectives"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Adjectives that end in <span class=\"strong\">-ing </span> are used to describe things and situations, like <span class=\"italic\">annoying</span>, <span class=\"italic\"> entertaining</span>, <span class=\"italic\"> surprising</span>, <span class=\"italic\"> worrying</span> or <span class=\"italic\">tiring</span>. These adjectives describe the <span class=\"strong\">effect </span>, something has on a person."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">The study is compelling.</span> (It makes me feel compelled).<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Work is sometimes surprising, too.</span> (It makes me feel tired)."}, {"type": "example", "content": "It was exciting, but it was very wholesome. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "We were never bored playing outside. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Used to and Would"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Would</span> and <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> have similar meanings. They are both used to describe something that happened regularly in the past but doesn't happen any longer. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "However, there is an important difference between <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> and <span class=\"strong\">would</span>.<br><br>   <span class=\"strong\">Would</span> is not used unless you know that the time frame is in the past, while <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> does not require this. <br><br>  Read the following example: <br>  <span class=\"italic\">We would visit India every summer when we were children.</span><br>  When we were children refers to a past time frame and therefore makes the meaning of would clear.<br><br>  <span class=\"italic\">We used to visit India every summer. </span><br>  Here, you do not have to include a past time frame since the meaning of <span class=\"strong\">used to</span> clear."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I used to go out with a guy before I left for culinary school."}, {"type": "example", "content": "When we were in high school, Ted would write me poems and send me flowers every week."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn7le08ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "How do you see dating in the future?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Discuss with a partner about whether you think dating will be different than it is today."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Be specific in your opinion. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use adjectives to add details to your opinion."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I consider how dating in the future might be different from dating today."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I discuss social activities with a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I give specific details about my opinion."}], "type": "takeaway_assessmen