 was younger, we didn't start dating until high school.  We used to spend more time playing with toys or being adventurous outside than we did thinking about the opposite sex. I think the mindset was very different than today. My friends and I would talk about boys, but our parents were much more protective of us and wouldn't allow us to go out alone with a boy. He would have to come over for dinner, meet our parents and even then, we would only be allowed to see each other for an hour or two. My friends used to sneak out of the house sometimes to meet up with their boyfriends ... it was exciting, but it was very wholesome.\"", "id": 2, "image": "engenn7le08ob07re2img01.jpg"}, {"time": "50000", "text": "\"The ease of access to personal e-mail and social media accounts gives kids no boundaries within which to function. They don't have the wisdom to know right from wrong at that point in their lives - being a teenager is about pushing boundaries and testing limits, right?\"", "id": 3, "image": "engenn7le08ob07re2img02.jpg"}], "coverimg": "engenn7le08ob07re2img05.jpg"}}], "template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "id": 1}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "id": 0}]}